Leading wildcards compile into the suffix set; mid-pattern wildcards are
parsed and counted as unsupported (v0.2 slow path).

-- list w block adblock --
*.cdn.example
*.track.example^
||*.ads.example^
||ad*.example^
*.*.example
||example.*^
-- counts w --
rules=3 unsupported=3 invalid=0 entries=3
-- expect --
cdn.example          block w *.cdn.example       # deviation: *.x also matches x (blocky semantics)
img.cdn.example      block w *.cdn.example
a.b.cdn.example      block w *.cdn.example
mycdn.example        pass
x.track.example      block w *.track.example
ads.example          block w ||*.ads.example^    # deviation: as above
x.ads.example        block w ||*.ads.example^
adserver.example     pass                        # mid-pattern wildcard: unsupported in v0.1
example.com          pass
